{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_DCM_SECTION_7_2_4_11_Manage_session_state","src":"manifest","doc":"SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager","page":68,"text":"7.2.4.11 Manage session state\n[SWS_Dcm_00022]\nUpstream requirements: RS_Diag_04006\n⌈The DSL submodule shall save the state of the current active session.⌋\nFor accessing this variable, the DSL submodule provides interfaces to:\n• get the current active session: Dcm_GetSesCtrlType\n• set a new session: DslInternal_SetSesCtrlType()\n[SWS_Dcm_00034]\nUpstream requirements: SRS_BSW_00101\n⌈During Dcm initialization, the session state is set to the value 0x01 (\"DefaultSession\").⌋\n[SWS_Dcm_01062] ⌈The call to Dcm_ResetToDefaultSession allows the appli-\ncation to reset the current session to Default session and invokes the mode switch\nof the ModeDeclarationGroupPrototype DcmDiagnosticSessionControl by calling\nSchM_Switch_<bsnp>_DcmDiagnosticSessionControl(RTE_MODE_DcmDiagnostic\nSessionControl_DCM_DEFAULT_SESSION).⌋\nExample: Automatic termination of an extended diagnostic session upon exceeding of\na speed limit.","caption":"7.2.4.11 Manage session state","sha":null,"series":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_DCM_SECTION_7_2_4_11_Manage_session_state","releases":["R25-11"],"page":68,"hash":"928dcabbc5b38892","caption":""}],"releases":["R25-11"],"trel":"R25-11","tstat":"section","kind":"snippet","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_Dcm_00022] im Text von SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager.","rel":["R25-11"],"id":"SWS_Dcm_00022"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_Dcm_00034] im Text von SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager.","rel":["R25-11"],"id":"SWS_Dcm_00034"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE (deterministic citation)","rel":["R25-11"],"id":"SWS_Dcm_00339"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","m":"g